{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"425","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Sereja and Table "}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sereja has an "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × m"},{"kind":"text","text":" rectangular table "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", each cell of the table contains a zero or a number one. Sereja wants his table to meet the following requirement: each connected component of the same values forms a rectangle with sides parallel to the sides of the table. Rectangles should be filled with cells, that is, if a component form a rectangle of size "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h × w"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the component must contain exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"hw"},{"kind":"text","text":" cells."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A connected component of the same values is a set of cells of the table that meet the following conditions:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" every two cells of the set have the same value; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the cells of the set form a connected region on the table (two cells are connected if they are adjacent in some row or some column of the table); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" it is impossible to add any cell to the set unless we violate the two previous conditions. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Can Sereja change the values of at most "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" cells of the table so that the table met the described requirement? What minimum number of table cells should he change in this case?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n, m ≤ 100; 1 ≤ k ≤ 10)"},{"kind":"text","text":". Next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines describe the table "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":": the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of them contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai1, ai2, ..., aim"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0 ≤ ai, j ≤ 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the values in the cells of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th row."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print -1, if it is impossible to meet the requirement. Otherwise, print the minimum number of cells which should be changed."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"tex